# pacman install scriptlet (#974). pacman runs this as root and cannot reach
# each user's home, so per-user data is removed by the user, not by pacman.
# The message only appears once the package is going: by then `okilum
# --uninstall-data` is gone too, so it lists the folders instead.

post_remove() {
    cat <<'MSG'
==> Okilum was removed. Your notes were not touched.
    If you did not run `okilum --uninstall-data` before, your per-user
    Okilum data is still in (default locations):
        ~/.local/state/okilum   ~/.config/okilum   ~/.cache/okilum
    Remove those folders to finish. If Sync was set up, remove this computer
    from Sync in Okilum first; its user service is okilum-syncthing-*.service.
MSG
}
